Parity reproduced exactly from the web source (cross-platform value parity, not a "corrected" version):
  Time       = formatTime(timestamp)  → locale 2-digit hour:minute; "—" when missing/unparseable
  Signal     = entry.name (monospaced)
  Value      = entry.value (monospaced), tinted by TYPE_VALUE_COLOR (number→cyan/string→green/boolean→amber)
  Type       = chip keyed by Badge variant (number→info, boolean→warning, string→success)
  Freshness  = <FreshnessIndicator>: dot fresh<120s/stale<600s/offline≥600s/unknown(nil) + formatAge label
               (nil→"—", <10s→"just now", <60s→"Ns ago", <3600s→"Nm ago", else "Nh ago")
  filtered   = filter ? entries.filter(name.toLowerCase().includes(filter.toLowerCase())) : entries   (NO trim)
  stats      = Signals/sec(rate) · Buffer Size(entries.length "/ bufferMax") · Unique Signals · Filtered(filtered.length)
  empty msg  = entries.length==0 ? "Waiting for signals…" : "No signals match filter"
  controls   = Pause/Resume (onPauseToggle) · Auto-scroll toggle (default on, pins newest) · Clear (onClear)

States reproduced (every one renders — no hidden surfaces; each has a #if DEBUG preview):
  loading (native chrome "Connecting…") · empty ("Waiting for signals…") · content (stats+table) ·
  filtered-empty ("No signals match filter") · error (native chrome + Retry) · stale (banner) · offline (banner) ·
  paused (chip + Resume).

